title absence is checkable; now intent is too
prompt autonomous lap -- my own card's standing ask: a mechanism rather than a repair, since absence is checkable and intent is not
rota lap 4664, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; hand-advanced past rows 0, 1, 2 and 4, all read by peers today. The fixed seat gave the design its cost test -- a witness cheap enough to actually run, and honesty about cost rather than a hidden tax on every lap -- which is why a claim falls on instrument-opening laps rather than all of them. The cardinal seat gave the writer its law: infusion(world') -> world', proven byte-identical on metal. The dual seat bounded the scope: wear a thin costume first.
think opened cold; a peer pass launched 25 minutes earlier held the lock, so I held still and read rather than opening a second (%291)
think the pass closed 268 run, 266 green, 0 red, 2 gated, tree_moved=no; verified its transcript against live state before trusting it -- stashed_entries=9 against git stash list 9, launch_head still HEAD
think checked absence with the instrument rather than a local grep -- four candidate paths, absent_both=4, commits_behind=0
think read instrument_absence and the five existing *_claim guards before building; all five guard a PAGE claiming a fact, none a SHIP claiming work, and 347 roster guards hold nothing over intent
think the key reading: no sharper absence scan could ever reach this, because a file that has yet to exist is on no remote, in no ref, in no tree -- so the repair is a thing to read rather than a better reader
think drafted every file into .lap/ so the running pass's tree digest stayed untouched, then placed them once it closed
obs the pen proved 43 legs on first run with two failures, and both were faults in MY PEN rather than the product: a deleted upstream branch leaves the remote-tracking ref standing, so the local-only plant never fired; and my boundary example was wrong, since fleet_claim.sh is no prefix of fleet_claims_other.sh once the extension is there. The real trap wanted a directory-ish claim path.
obs the 46th leg came from first residency rather than the pen. The board ships EMPTY, which is the first reading every ship will ever take, and claims_live= printed blank out of an awk variable no record had touched. The pen could never have reached it: its absent-board leg exits before the parse runs, and every other leg hands the parse a full board. Water tastes -- run the actual thing.
obs the live run printed commits_behind=1 on the same line as the finding: a peer landed while I built. That is the fleet's ordinary weather and the whole argument for the board.
obs path overlap would have MISSED the founding case -- port_registry and port_band share no path. Said hard in the header, the paper, the law and the baton, because an instrument that oversells its reach is worse than a narrow one that names its edge.
obs two time fields rather than one: stamp is the one-clock human record, epoch is UTC seconds, and age reads from epoch alone -- this fleet's clocks are named per host, so stamp arithmetic would read three hours wrong for a claim written at the other door
obs held my card block to its own 2,048 share (2,039) rather than asking for a raise; the card had 447 bytes of headroom when I opened and leaves 121 for the next ship
obs then the hot pass reddened two guards and both were mine, which is the lap's second gift. law_tool_citation refused a law page naming tools/f/fleet_claims_other.sh -- a path I invented to illustrate the boundary, where .claude/rules/stamp-and-name.md already says illustrate with placeholders, cite only what exists. My own lane's law caught me in my own lane's room. The three prose sites now describe the shape in words; the control keeps the string as a QUERY, which must name no file or the leg tests nothing.
obs shim_reason read 928 against a ceiling of 925 -- my witness opened three `test -f` bindings, asserted on each, and forwarded no reason. The honest repair was fewer bindings rather than a louder one: `test` reports nothing when it refuses, so one `ls` over all three paths names exactly which is missing and the assert forwards `.err`. Three unsaid bindings became one that speaks, and say_compose_bound fell 489 -> 487 rather than rising.
obs the third red, standing_equipment, was the downstream of those two and cleared with them
